# Wire existing data on shipped screens

We build on the previous slice. Leaving a shipped screen stale is a failed slice, not later work.

If the locked design shows a field, and this repo already stores that value, the UI must show the real value. Do not hardcode `"—"`, `"0"`, a fake name, or empty text for data this repo already has.

A later ticket is only for data this version does not have yet (for example open repairs before work orders exist, rent before rent is stored).

When a slice creates or links a record, open every shipped screen that already displays a related column or label and wire it in that same slice. `"—"` is allowed only when that row truly has no value.
